# Quaternion placement in outer involution centralizers of PSL₃(4)

The development supplies full standard automorphism coverage, faithful
conjugation transport and quaternion placement for the field, graph and
graph-field representatives and their conjugates. The concrete field and
graph Sylow models and the graph-field centralizer map discharge every
structural premise of the representative placement theorems.

All carriers are the actual projective matrix group and its automorphism
group. The transport preserves automorphism order, outer status, full
centralizers, and the actual conjugation image.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.4(4)–(6), printed p.1171, and the
quaternion placement used in the proof of 16.4.9(2), printed p.1192.
-/
